 is $42{\\text{ cm}}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 42 & =\\frac{7\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\ 7CD & =84 \\\\ CD & =12\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overset{―}{CD}$ is also the height of $△ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/0014faf05eaf15d70f885802e5b820b0c72d42a96f400442f827ed229de8b240.png)\n\nTherefore, we find the area of $△ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 12}{2} \\\\  & =30{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-87910/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87910"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117374/selection/5a8aa359ab2392ab4406daf5471d51612ab613871418bd90366919e9eaef9940" :answer/id #uuid "742e1daa-d481-5df7-9ca6-9b2b1c89b36c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117374/selection/6de0ddc2150297ee7b476e34bc103489c937df15004f1bfff5dd1a09b55f50df" :answer/id #uuid "568854ca-c43b-5d15-befc-8d1ffe985593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117374/selection/95db16b4c338a4df4de0a8d22356f1c53d0fbd9feb4f2c7b2f1b02bcf22956fe" :answer/id #uuid "65367e9d-4ee2-5f36-851c-39758476675e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117374/selection/801977bc3d8de6116816b6a1c8b8a868de659348ed01cd17e80f15c0e701618c" :answer/id #uuid "7f89799e-4e6c-5dfc-a5a8-85b394aefb0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117374/selection/8104bcf64ed317b8b7a3d6d226587c474c875f5047c4e0e59411d3696266c6d7" :answer/id #uuid "3bbd7008-9c99-5dec-90b3-74724de488d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117374/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a450a329-d5cd-527f-9d2f-b92ac44d1261" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117374/selection/6de0ddc2150297ee7b476e34bc103489c937df15004f1bfff5dd1a09b55f50df" :answer-field/choices ["q-117374/selection/5a8aa359ab2392ab4406daf5471d51612ab613871418bd90366919e9eaef9940" "q-117374/selection/6de0ddc2150297ee7b476e34bc103489c937df15004f1bfff5dd1a09b55f50df" "q-117374/selection/95db16b4c338a4df4de0a8d22356f1c53d0fbd9feb4f2c7b2f1b02bcf22956fe" "q-117374/selection/801977bc3d8de6116816b6a1c8b8a868de659348ed01cd17e80f15c0e701618c" "q-117374/selection/8104bcf64ed317b8b7a3d6d226587c474c875f5047c4e0e59411d3696266c6d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117374" :question/id #uuid "8450a28f-9fa7-54f9-a61c-39e7c40a3f14" :question/math-academy-id "q-117374" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/45d1ad7a8cf54a09c2605e2afd3af415de4e42726923bf4771af79aa66079f05.png)\n\nFind $AB$ given that the area of $△ABC$ is $140\\,{m}^{2}$ and $CH=14\\,m.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is $b=AB,$ and the corresponding height is \n\n$$\nh=CH=14\\,m.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the formula for the area, we can solve for the base as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 140 & =\\frac{b\\cdot 14}{2} \\\\ 280 & =b\\cdot 14 \\\\ b & =\\frac{280}{14} \\\\ b & =20\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $AB=20\\,\\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117374/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117374"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117356/selection/95db16b4c338a4df4de0a8d22356f1c53d0fbd9feb4f2c7b2f1b02bcf22956fe" :answer/id #uuid "e95b7857-a2b3-528c-b0ac-5577c1ee1d1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117356/selection/b17cdd382181bc13c481e4da515714b280ffa0c7d469d9d7c6ab7ec514f49a27" :answer/id #uuid "f8248279-d0d8-5cc9-b109-d775eb59db85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117356/selection/ca28a82dc9cb2031b675149fe9bba251523526e2b468d345bef50c9dfd4da534" :answer/id #uuid "b750770d-28f8-5052-a46b-9c91524753ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117356/selection/0fd72835397f5ba06fbb553ab6bd2a2316356327e6c48b899f68d32d4605a61b" :answer/id #uuid "74a6c9f1-77c5-5dc0-9464-9cd29fe23947" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117356/selection/99b06975eb4f744a14bbc1aee4ee385e1a08c59641f259f5f6e85761cce18677" :answer/id #uuid "d012c751-ac5d-5125-b9b6-cda3e0d86790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117356/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5043b17-ebe0-57ee-80ec-5aab94ccabec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117356/selection/99b06975eb4f744a14bbc1aee4ee385e1a08c59641f259f5f6e85761cce18677" :answer-field/choices ["q-117356/selection/95db16b4c338a4df4de0a8d22356f1c53d0fbd9feb4f2c7b2f1b02bcf22956fe" "q-117356/selection/b17cdd382181bc13c481e4da515714b280ffa0c7d469d9d7c6ab7ec514f49a27" "q-117356/selection/ca28a82dc9cb2031b675149fe9bba251523526e2b468d345bef50c9dfd4da534" "q-117356/selection/0fd72835397f5ba06fbb553ab6bd2a2316356327e6c48b899f68d32d4605a61b" "q-117356/selection/99b06975eb4f744a14bbc1aee4ee385e1a08c59641f259f5f6e85761cce18677"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117356" :question/id #uuid "4303d1bd-0440-58eb-a5d5-e6551f7a6e46" :question/math-academy-id "q-117356" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/10b6f63df56c789d0d28cd14caad0a2588e247ba4a60239f4cb0dd5a32777daf.png)\n\nFind $AM$ given that the area of $△ABC$ is $64\\,{m}^{2},$ $MC=11\\,m,$ and $BM=8\\,m.$}\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is $b=AC,$ and the corresponding height is \n\n$$\nh=BM=8\\,m.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the formula for the area, we can solve for the base as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 64 & =\\frac{b\\cdot 8}{2} \\\\ 128 & =b\\cdot 8 \\\\ b & =\\frac{128}{8} \\\\ b & =16\\,m\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $AC=16\\,m$ and hence, we have\n\n$$\nAM=AC-MC=16-11=5\\,\\text{m}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117356/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117356"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117365/selection/ae5eca91d0a5c570e7fff531ebe5c52d400d02dbb5b2dbab62e525731dbd4777" :answer/id #uuid "d5bb2628-1bb2-5b4f-a5a0-8b3dbf59f09a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117365/selection/05ce2f8de39209d31ff93348011769891a92e26df96d9c21cd1647363a0ff28a" :answer/id #uuid "048d8d61-7908-5cf0-8096-82fd4425c783" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117365/selection/358bb956e978b3f6263e926348f4d527c9c784bb19a3bc0aeffbcc97f7aecc79" :answer/id #uuid "f67e787d-757a-50dd-90e9-7c10c9a1f995" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117365/selection/0a0fd2e33cb744c2a6746aea10a1d207ac6b4d7d1453fd3da2970078a8515c73" :answer/id #uuid "e6accb97-5480-52e9-931b-b2880998af09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117365/selection/91a7048aac87e5299e73ef96016fd4251c0780c198432892ac7b0e50c94aa9d5" :answer/id #uuid "2c092507-9ec5-5d2c-bcb4-98b045e089a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117365/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f73c6ce-729a-571b-a4f2-a88cabcb062d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117365/selection/0a0fd2e33cb744c2a6746aea10a1d207ac6b4d7d1453fd3da2970078a8515c73" :answer-field/choices ["q-117365/selection/ae5eca91d0a5c570e7fff531ebe5c52d400d02dbb5b2dbab62e525731dbd4777" "q-117365/selection/05ce2f8de39209d31ff93348011769891a92e26df96d9c21cd1647363a0ff28a" "q-117365/selection/358bb956e978b3f6263e926348f4d527c9c784bb19a3bc0aeffbcc97f7aecc79" "q-117365/selection/0a0fd2e33cb744c2a6746aea10a1d207ac6b4d7d1453fd3da2970078a8515c73" "q-117365/selection/91a7048aac87e5299e73ef96016fd4251c0780c198432892ac7b0e50c94aa9d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117365" :question/id #uuid "c457037c-f30c-55b6-9f52-d739e0d113b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-117365" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945897/assets/4310195e821f7c09399073a2b4eb3e10c262ad61cbb3fe8d951645caee51a4d0.png)\n\nConsider the triangles $△ABC$ and $△BCD$ shown above. If the area of $△BCD$ is $42{\\text{ in}}^{2}$, find the area of $△ABC.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider $△BCD.$ We can see that $\\overset{―}{BC}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{CD}$ and that $CD=12\\text{ in}.$ \n\nSince the area of $△BCD$ is $42{\\text{ in}}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 42 & =\\frac{CD\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\ 42 & =\\frac{12\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\ 84 & =12\\cdot BC \\\\ BC & =\\frac{84}{12} \\\\ BC & =7\\text{ in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overset{―}{BC}$ is also the height of $△ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Therefore, we find the area of $△ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{2} \\\\  & =17.5{\\text{ in}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117365/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117365"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
